## 2. PMASK_NO_SELFMASK=1, redact mode: the escape is overridden after the fork
pmask: warning: PMASK_NO_SELFMASK=1 is overridden in redact mode: the supervisor masks its own /proc entry after the fork, so secret 'T' (literal:) is readable in its argv or environment only until then, not for the whole run; keep the command out of the supervisor's argv with --args-from-fd, or use file:PATH or agent:NAME
20 samples, samples with the secret: 2; last: proc-evid|

## 3. PMASK_NO_SELFMASK=1, plain mode: the escape is honoured
pmask: warning: PMASK_NO_SELFMASK=1 leaves this process's own /proc entry readable for the whole run in plain mode, so secret 'T' (literal:) is in its argv or environment the entire time; every local account can read it.  Keep the command out of the supervisor's argv with --args-from-fd, or use file:PATH or agent:NAME
